    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (82.49) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) headlining our offensive attack. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier force, leveraging an elite 0.476 xwOBA against Janson Junk, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from the confluence of a #1 lineup spot and a favorable breeze blowing out, which boosts his already high ceiling against Jack Flaherty. **Christian Yelich** (74.24) is another vital engine; his matchup against Freddy Peralta is particularly compelling because of the potential for base-stealing opportunities against a pitcher prone to slower deliveries, a key metric given our aggressive focus on stolen bases. **Colt Keith** (69.64) also presents excellent value, with his score bolstered by favorable wind conditions and a strong spot in the heart of the order.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Nelson Velazquez**, who remains on the bench with a 51.27 score despite a solid xwOBA of 0.394 against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the specific lineup positioning of **Lars Nootbaar** and the defensive-efficiency floor of our starters over the upside provided by **Nelson Velazquez**. We remain cautious regarding **Junior Caminero** (56.76); while he possesses significant talent, drawing Dylan Cease\u2014the toughest arm on our docket with an xERA of 2.96\u2014suppresses his overall score. Furthermore, owners should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players; while we have projected these starts based on historical trends, any late shifts in batting orders\u2014particularly for **Dillon Dingler** or **Kyle Schwarber**\u2014could necessitate a last-minute re-evaluation of our efficiency thresholds.",
